From: ReadyNAS NG <readynasng@build>
Subject: [PATCH 01/27] sparc: add the Infrant IT3107 "Padre" platform

The NETGEAR ReadyNAS Duo v1 runs on the Infrant IT3107 "Padre", a
SPARC v8 SoC with its own MMU, no PROM and no FPU; NETGEAR only ever
shipped a 2.6.17 kernel for it. This adds CONFIG_SPARC_PADRE and the
platform core, rewritten for 6.18 from NETGEAR's GPL 2.6.17 sources:

- Kconfig option (sparc32, !SMP), LEON excluded, CMDLINE_BOOL allowed;
- asm/padre.h: register map, ASIs, boot parameters;
- head_32.S: iboot does "go 0x80004000" with no PROM: turn the MMU
  fixed windows and the caches on, then continue the stock boot path;
  kernel linked at 0x80004000 (KERNBASE 0x80000000);
- padre_prom.c: minimal OpenBoot PROM emulated from iboot's boot_param
  (romvec, device tree, polled console, command line);
- padre_kernel.c: interrupt controller and timer (irq_chip,
  sparc_config), padre.disable= to switch drivers off;
- cpu/setup/irq/process/ioport glue: sparc_padre CPU model, no FPU
  probe, busy idle (the Padre has no sleep mode), ioremap() through the
  fixed I/O window, D-cache invalidation for DMA.

Not buildable alone: the MMU code (next patch) is required.
